  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "An integrated evaluation framework was developed to assess OpenStreetMap 3D building data quality by pairing 3D geometric comparisons with machine learning predictions. Tested on over 115,000 buildings across six cities in Asia and Europe—Beijing, Ningbo, Osaka, Yokohama, Amsterdam, and Almere—the model uses footprint Intersection over Union and centroid distances to pair crowd-sourced structures with official reference datasets, evaluating spatial precision through height, location, surface area, and 3D Hausdorff distance metrics.",
      "why": "This framework moves beyond 2D footprint analyses to evaluate actual 3D building characteristics like facade geometry and height, allowing researchers to flag quality issues across incomplete mapping datasets where reference geometry is missing."
